      "publishes": "atrium.car.height",
      "guard": "body-in-travel",
      "clearance": 0.01,
      "note": "The glass car on the Elan axis. Body frame = its floor datum on the axis at the Atrium stop; range = the body's offset along +z at fractions 0 and 1 (-23.600 ... +20.400), stops as fractions of 44.000 m. Drive: rack and pinion on the two guide rails above the Cube's clamp level (pinions in the roller-guide blocks, both rings; the rails' breaks at the seams and the collar are bridged by the second ring); below the clamp level the car hangs on the Cube mast its crown feeds out; above the Sphere's mouth it rides the Sphere's mast (the Sphere's, rising from its mouth). No counterweight. Jerk-limited S-curves (<= 1.0 m/s3). Leaves shut before any move (they wait while a body stands in the doorway). Interlocks A-1...A-7 in the sheet (section 6). Home: the neck stop with both neck irises shut (as built); with atrium.up unmated the home is the Atrium stop and the collar iris stays shut; with atrium.down unmated nothing goes below the Atrium stop. Left open at the Atrium with nobody within r 3.500 (or off the floor) for 12 s, the car runs 'close' (home). It never lands in the Cube (no landing, door or vestibule there): it stops with the eyes at the Cube's centre and its light falls to a glimmer. Steps {move: <stop>} name a stop. Stops' z are notes (at decides). Travel z −23.600 → +20.400. Default drive on the rails; the zone 0 → 0.290341 is the Cube mast."
    },
